Audited the exact local SFT copy designated as `alpharomercoma/AndroidAgent-SFT-v4@570febb36b3ee2ed6b11c72653a1abee62744f5d`: 94,861 train rows and 2,265 dev rows. Audited the cached RL snapshot `alpharomercoma/AndroidAgent-RL-v4@586c241b8b454a89f1803cf523d18d514cd34b08`, including its content hash; live Hub rechecking was unavailable. Source HEAD stayed `0d362dfb61225ed457f617f76e9e59a8961b92c2`. Existing files and processes were unchanged; all reproductions were CPU-only and used synthetic outcomes. [Scope/hashes](v4_data_audit/audit_scope.json), [artifact hashes](v4_data_audit/image_integrity.json), [RL identity](v4_data_audit/rl_cache_identity.json).

1. **P1 — STOP: final-goal verification still admits incorrect supervision.** `11564#qa` asks Gwalior arrival: gold **21:02 is departure; arrival is 21:00** ([qa06](v4_data_audit/samples/qa06.png), train shard 00, row 5470). `5056#qa` labels a selected shoe size **UK**, which is the sizing system; no size is selected ([qa49](v4_data_audit/samples/qa49.png)). `278#qa` assigns neighboring colourways' **Out of Stock** labels to the selected colourway, with a false rationale claiming all images carry that label ([qa52](v4_data_audit/samples/qa52.png)). Another question asks for a bus departure on a walking/train itinerary. Separately, **9/60 goals disclose their answer**, and **7/60 conflict with navigation/context**. Dev episode `2502#qa` invents the app “Amigo” from a banner advertisement. Pass 2 verifies answer agreement on the screenshot; it does not reliably verify app identity, navigation constraints or compound-goal leakage. All four sampled bad train QA labels are in the RL pool. [Per-row judgments](v4_data_audit/visual_review.tsv), [exact prompts/rationales](v4_data_audit/samples.json), [RL row mapping](v4_data_audit/cross_counts.json).

2. **P1 — STOP: stable app inventories are frequently incomplete.** Exact known app names followed by “app” in goals are absent from the actual Installed apps line in **23,100/94,861 train rows**, including **988/2,835 unique QA endpoints (34.9%)**; also 62/162 dev_answer and 52/135 dev_complete rows. Example: qa52 explicitly requests the Nike app, but Nike is absent. `data/v4_build_parquet.py:101–115` collects structured `open_app` targets; sampled histories can omit app opening altogether. The list is stable but contradicts the task. Counts are a bounded lexical census, with aliases/invented names requiring adjudication. [Exact goals, lists and locations](v4_data_audit/missing_named_apps.json).

3. **P1 — STOP under the declared protocol: guard v2 still admits excluded apps.** There are **205 train QA endpoints explicitly mentioning Gmail/Drive/Maps/YouTube** in goals/history, or **226 including excluded app types**; 15 dev candidates match the wider scan. Reviewed examples confirm Gmail use and Google Drive screens (qa04/15/16/40). The guard examines structured app-opening names and a partial term list on the original goal, missing clicked share targets and rewritten goals (`v4_build_parquet.py:131–151`). Fifty-one RL QA states also match this exposure scan. This establishes guard failure and same-app exposure, **not copied benchmark tasks**. No full-template or eight-word fixed-span matches were found against 57 static AW templates, 25 IR prompts and 18 dynamic-goal literal forms; paraphrases/runtime compositions remain outside that check. [Exposure candidates](v4_data_audit/aw_exposure_candidates.json), [template scan](v4_data_audit/aw_template_scan_extended.json).

4. **P1 — HOLD RL: the reward can be maximized with substantively wrong answers.** All 18 shipped reward fixtures pass. Actual-pool probes nevertheless give reward **1.0 for `12M → 12`** (row 1772), **`22K → 22`** (36), **`Oct 4 → 4`** (1007), and times without AM/PM. `v4_answer_check.py:43–48` permits dropping all words after preserving digit tokens. Numeric-only stripping scores 1 on 391/700 QA states; many unit omissions are legitimate, so **391 is not an error count**. The counterexamples establish magnitude/date corruption. The same comparator is used by the SFT agreement check and development gate; no month/AM-PM/magnitude loss caused specifically by `preferred()` was found in the built endpoints. [Real-pool attacks](v4_data_audit/rl_actual_answer_attacks.json), [fixtures/adversarial cases](v4_data_audit/reward_probes.json).

5. **P1 — Evaluation success markers remain untrustworthy.** Synthetic runner exit 42 still produces exit 0 and “v4 AndroidWorld seed-30 finished” in `local_v4_to_aw.sh:34–38`. `vm_rl_go.sh` returns 0 and “RL PIPELINE DONE” when **all five dev evals, AC eval and uploads fail**. The corrected gate rejects zero accuracy, but passes fabricated dev keys/GT and 113 fabricated task names plus three real answer-task names: it checks matching counts, not frozen identities/seed/model. These failures invalidate automatic promotion, not the measured training loss. [Executable reproductions](v4_data_audit/wrapper_reproductions.json).

6. **P1 operational risk — RL smoke can contend with running SFT.** `vm_rl_hook.sh:7` starts the launcher on upload; `vm_rl_go.sh:17` starts GPU smoke **before** waiting for SFT completion at line 28. The advertised contention avoidance therefore does not cover smoke. No actual OOM was observed. Move smoke behind the wait before launching this pilot. [Source and remaining RL checks](v4_data_audit/technical_notes.md).

7. **P2 — ScreenQA shortening and requested answer formats still need cleanup.** ScreenQA09 drops `- CA` from a provider entity; ScreenQA27's `Home` is not visible (inherited from the original). ScreenQA17/18 drop another selected tab. Several QA/dev gold answers include units or words despite “just the number” (qa15/43/46, dev01/02/03/11). Reasoning strings are structurally valid but include the false visual claims in finding 1. [Original-versus-shortened judgments](v4_data_audit/visual_review.json).

8. **P2 — Dev controls and metrics can mislead.** `dev_complete` still includes “I need to know” exchange-rate goals (episode 13412, row 43; 17404, row 109), despite its action-only claim. Train-derived dev provenance is now disclosed, but these episodes were present in v3 training. The RL launcher uses `score_dev.py`'s token-F1 ≥0.5 criterion: synthetic `no alerts → alerts`, `$10 → €10`, `-5 → 5` all score correct. It neither enforces the seed-30 gate nor an adopted numeric RL promotion rule. Existing SFT eval cache checks also omit prompt/pool identity. [Dev goals](v4_data_audit/dev_complete_goals.json), [metric probes](v4_data_audit/evaluation_metric_probes.json), [details](v4_data_audit/technical_notes.md).

9. **P2 — Remaining RL/rebuild risks.** The four-step base-model timing is not a hard budget; minimum ten steps can exceed the requested allowance, and waits/evals/uploads are unbounded. Reload smoke never asserts action parseability. A second CUDA model loads while the trainer remains resident. Package versions/config compatibility and useful reward variance are not enforced. Case-insensitive `input_text` reward accepts all 43 capitalization-bearing pool inputs after lowercasing; some are harmless, but case-sensitive text is unsafe. Coordinate reward is only distance to one point. AC test revision is unpinned. Teacher restart/ScreenQA checkpoint weaknesses persist for a rebuild. [Evidence and limitations](v4_data_audit/technical_notes.md).

I visually inspected **119 extracted PNGs**: the requested 60 QA, 30 shortened ScreenQA and 20 dev_answer, plus nine coverage supplements. QA selection used six random endpoints per original question/compound × number/price/date-time/name/phrase stratum. ScreenQA/dev primary samples were simple random; seeds and every judgment are recorded. Supplements are excluded from these rates. “Answer error” includes wrong, ungrounded or incomplete answers; “any issue” additionally includes question ambiguity, goal leakage or navigation mismatch, but excludes the separate app-inventory census.

| Primary sample | Answer errors, Wilson 95% CI | Any issue, Wilson 95% CI |
|---|---:|---:|
| QA, 60 | 4/60 = **6.7% [2.6%, 15.9%]** | 20/60 = **33.3% [22.7%, 45.9%]** |
| Shortened ScreenQA, 30 | 2/30 = **6.7% [1.8%, 21.3%]** | 4/30 = **13.3% [5.3%, 29.7%]** |
| dev_answer, 20 | 0/20 = **0% [0%, 16.1%]** | 1/20 = **5.0% [0.9%, 23.6%]** |

QA's pooled interval describes the deliberately balanced sample. Reweighting to the 2,835-endpoint population gives **4.2% answer errors**, approximate stratified 95% CI **[1.3%, 22.9%]**; any-issue estimate **38.9% [25.5%, 55.0%]**. Small stratum samples give wide uncertainty. [Sampling/statistics](v4_data_audit/visual_review.json), [method](v4_data_audit/technical_notes.md).

Each prior P1 was rechecked against current code and, where applicable, the built artifact:

| Prior P1 | Closure result |
|---|---|
| 1. Gate zero accuracy/missing inputs | **Partial:** numeric threshold, counts and single-run checks fixed; frozen task/dev/seed/model identities still unvalidated. |
| 2. Sealed outcome logging | **Closed for v2:** synthetic outcome stays sealed; stdout exposes failure/count only. Older runner use remains a documented deviation; its outcomes were not read. |
| 3. Teacher answer agreement | **Original examples closed:** all five old bad pairs reject; all retained labels pass current check. Semantic numeric omissions remain open, especially for RL. |
| 4. ScreenQA validator/build failure | **Partial:** all 1,233 built shortenings pass shared validation; old decimal/negation/comma cases reject. Semantic completeness remains open. |
| 5. Exact eventual question | **Partial:** all 17,012 QA-row goals match current construction; direct goals have matching second answers. Full-goal correctness/leakage remains open. |
| 6. AW guard | **Partial:** all four old Settings episodes are excluded; 169 labels rejected. New bypasses remain in the artifact. |
| 7. False runner completion | **Partial:** sealed v2 rejects exit 42/0 episodes; development handoff still reports success. |

[Builder closure evidence](v4_data_audit/builder_closure.json), [wrapper evidence](v4_data_audit/wrapper_reproductions.json).

Controls that passed: all **97,126** rows have the exact v4 system prompt, one Installed apps line, correct roles, valid target JSON and string reasoning; all image bytes match `img_sha`. App lists are stable per episode. **Zero exact dev/train image overlap** and no held-out dev-episode reuse. All 2,835 QA endpoints have correct duplication: original question ×4 / compound ×2; 22 question-to-compound fallbacks retain original-kind ×4 weighting. Rolling histories have the expected last-eight indices. [Structural census](v4_data_audit/structure.json), [history/pool invariants](v4_data_audit/additional_invariants.json).

RL pool construction also passes: exact deterministic 2,000-row membership, unchanged system/user prompts and images, no dev-image leakage or duplicated QA weighting. GRPO's `image`/conversational `prompt`, thinking flag, fresh language-only LoRA on merged v4, v4 KL reference, beta 0.001, LR 1e-5 and bs4/ga8/gens4 agree with [TRL 1.16](https://github.com/huggingface/trl/blob/v1.16.0/trl/trainer/grpo_trainer.py) and [Liquid's example](https://github.com/Liquid4All/cookbook/blob/main/finetuning/notebooks/lfm3_vl_grpo_with_trl.ipynb). These are source-level checks, not a verified GPU run. [Pool verification](v4_data_audit/rl_pool_verification.json), [configuration detail](v4_data_audit/technical_notes.md).

Resume only after rebuilding and re-auditing the full goals/labels, complete app inventories and app exclusions. Preserve this run as a development artifact if useful. Repair reward semantics and failure/promotion checks before spending the RL budget.
