+STOP
+
+The rebuild still contains incorrect supervision and excluded-app exposure. Recommend stopping this SFT run and holding RL. **I did not interrupt training or modify existing files.**
+
+Audited the user-designated exact local SFT `alpharomercoma/AndroidAgent-SFT-v4@337553984ee970a767dceb21adc6343f3d613602`: **92,229 train rows; 2,184 dev rows; 2,386 unique train QA endpoints**, at source HEAD `449355f`. [Scope/hashes](v4b_reaudit/audit_scope.json).
+
+**RL scope limitation:** `alpharomercoma/AndroidAgent-RL-v4@9ba36d90abe9bdbaa0c578879336472ab054cc2c` was absent from the local cache; Hub access failed on DNS. RL results below use the builder's deterministic **2,000-state replay from the rebuilt SFT artifact**. The replay reproduces all 2,000 positions of the older cached pool, but the new published pool's bytes/membership remain unverified. [Access failure](v4b_reaudit/rl_hub_identity.json), [replay verification](v4b_reaudit/rl_pool_verification.json), [calibration](v4b_reaudit/rl_replay_calibration.json).
+
+1. **Partially closed — wrong answers/full goals.** The build drops 134 literal leaks, including seven of the nine previous sampled leaks. **All four previous bad QA labels survive unchanged**: `11564#qa` still labels Gwalior departure 21:02 as arrival instead of 21:00; `5056#qa` calls the sizing system UK a selected size; `278#qa` assigns neighboring colourways' stock status to the selected shoe; `17560#qa` asks for a bus departure on a walking/rail itinerary. Leaks `7,000` versus goal `7000`, and `picturesque Lake Bled` versus `Lake Bled`, remain. Dev `2502#qa` still invents Amigo from an advertisement. One cached direct-verifier approval (`396#qa`) now fails the revised comparator. [Retained rows](v4b_reaudit/prior_sample_presence.json), [rechecked screenshots](v4b_reaudit/followup_visual_review.json), [stale approval](v4b_reaudit/stale_direct_verification.json).
+
+2. **Partially closed — app inventories.** The identical lexical census falls from 23,100 to **5,518/92,229 train rows**, including **179/2,386 QA endpoints**; dev_answer **13/136**, dev_complete **4/80**, dev_odyssey **126/1,000**. `15271#qa` requests Adidas, shows Adidas shoes, and omits Adidas from Installed apps. Goal-name collection is case-sensitive and precedes teacher rewrites. Counts are lexical candidates: aliases and incorrect goal app names require adjudication. [Census](v4b_reaudit/missing_named_apps.json), [confirmed example](v4b_reaudit/inventory_adidas.json).
+
+3. **Partially closed — AW-app guard.** Same scanner: **70 train / 4 dev QA candidates**, previously 226/15; restricting to Gmail/Drive/Maps/YouTube gives **53/2**, previously 205/12. Adding “Drive app” yields 73/4. Screenshots confirm retained [Gmail](v4b_reaudit/samples/aw_gmail.png), [Drive](v4b_reaudit/samples/aw_drive.png), and [Google Maps](v4b_reaudit/samples/qa31.png). Lowercase app names and rewritten goals bypass the guard; image-only exposure also escapes the text census. **23/700 replayed RL QA states** match the original scanner. No full-template/eight-word matches against the same 100 static/IR/dynamic-literal forms; this establishes app exposure, not copied benchmark tasks. [Scan](v4b_reaudit/aw_exposure_candidates.json), [templates](v4b_reaudit/aw_template_scan_extended.json).
+
+4. **Partially closed — reward attacks.** Previous `12M→12`, `22K→22`, month/AM-PM/%/GB stripping fixtures now score 0; all 18 shipped reward fixtures pass. Replayed pool counterexamples still score **1.0**: row **1285**, `INR8,109.08→€8,109.08`; row **428**, `5:00p→5:00`; row **597**, `12M→12M is incorrect`. Appending `is incorrect` earns full reward on **639/700 QA states**. Changed numeric-only stripping succeeds on **305/431 attempts** among those 700 states; this is **not an error count**. The comparator recognizes neither all currency/time forms nor unrestricted added contradictory words. [Targeted attacks](v4b_reaudit/targeted_real_state_attacks.json), [full attacks](v4b_reaudit/rl_answer_attacks.json), [fixtures](v4b_reaudit/checker_and_reward_fixtures.json).
+
+5. **Partially closed — success markers/gate.** RL evaluation/upload failure accounting is fixed: the reproduction now exits **1**, recording ten failures. The development AW wrapper still turns runner exit **42** into exit **0** and “finished.” The gate still passes 113 fabricated task names plus three real answer tasks, wrong seed/model, and fabricated dev identities/GT using the new 136/80 counts. [Executable reproductions](v4b_reaudit/wrapper_reproductions.json).
+
+6. **Partially closed — SFT/RL contention.** `SKIP_SMOKE=1` can reuse an earlier marker, but missing/disabled reuse still starts GPU smoke **before** waiting for SFT (`vm_rl_go.sh:17–35`). The cached marker is not bound to current code/data. Actual VM skip state and contention were not verified; no OOM is claimed. [Source evidence](v4b_reaudit/technical_notes.md).
+
+7. **Open — ScreenQA/answer formats.** All 1,233 shortenings remain; the provider's missing `- CA`, unsupported `Home`, and dropped second selected tabs are unchanged on reinspection. New sample qa29/31/32/39 still adds words/units/currency despite number-only instructions. [Prior examples](v4b_reaudit/followup_visual_review.json), [new judgments](v4b_reaudit/visual_review.tsv).
+
+8. **Partially closed — dev controls/metrics.** Old controls 13412/17404 are removed and dev_complete shrinks to 80, but row **59**, episode **9070**, remains “curious about the actual exchange rate,” with gold `complete`. Strict comparison and a numeric RL promotion rule were added. However, “strict” metrics accept two concatenated action objects, score `status infeasible` as completion, and accept empty splits with exit 0. The launcher does not enforce promotion; train-derived dev provenance and prompt/pool cache-identity gaps remain. [Control screenshot](v4b_reaudit/samples/dev_information.png), [metric reproductions](v4b_reaudit/strict_metrics_probes.json), [details](v4b_reaudit/technical_notes.md).
+
+9. **Partially closed — remaining RL/rebuild risks.** Case-sensitive typing is fixed: **0/36** capitalization-changing attacks are rewarded. `grpo_vlm.py` is unchanged: reload output is never asserted parseable, a second CUDA model loads with the trainer resident, and dependency/configuration compatibility and useful reward variance remain unchecked. Estimated timing still forces at least ten steps without a hard deadline; point-distance reward, unpinned AC test, teacher restart and ScreenQA checkpoint gaps remain. [Typing attacks](v4b_reaudit/rl_input_text_attacks.json), [budget probes](v4b_reaudit/strict_metrics_probes.json), [source detail](v4b_reaudit/technical_notes.md).
+
+I visually inspected **40 QA endpoints**, seed **2026111802**, four per original question/compound × number/price/date-time/name/phrase stratum, with exact goals, histories and rationales. Ten overlap the prior sample because rare strata are small; no replacement after viewing. Targeted followups are excluded from these rates.
+
+| Measure | Count / rate | Wilson 95% CI |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| Answer error, including unsupported attribute | **4/40 — 10.0%** | **4.0–23.1%** |
+| Goal leakage | **2/40 — 5.0%** | **1.4–16.5%** |
+| Confirmed navigation mismatch | **1/40 — 2.5%** | **0.4–12.9%** |
+
+Errors: qa02 confuses the player's right-end runtime with current playback position; qa08 treats PDF body text as filename; qa09 treats shop sales as item sales; qa36 calls UK a size. Leaks: qa25 supplies the resort name, qa35 supplies Lake Bled. Navigation: qa31 requests transit but shows driving guidance. Ambiguous reminder referents and unverified sharing payloads are excluded from the navigation count. These Wilson intervals describe the **balanced sample**, not corpus prevalence; population-weighted estimates and uncertainty are in [visual_review.json](v4b_reaudit/visual_review.json).
+
+Controls passed: all **94,413** image hashes, system prompts, roles and target JSON; stable episode app lists; correct QA duplication; no exact train/dev image or held-out-episode overlap. Builder acceptance exactly reproduces **99 strict rejects + 500 guard rejects + 134 leak rejects**, leaving 2,522 train/dev QA endpoints. These structural passes do not close the semantic failures above. [Structure](v4b_reaudit/structure.json), [image integrity](v4b_reaudit/image_integrity.json), [builder replay](v4b_reaudit/builder_closure.json).
