index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..baed26fcd8a6cc7bbc8da5726fd3712f9b00e8ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/results/codex/v4b_reaudit/technical_notes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+Targeted v4b audit, 2026-11-18. All parquet and RL row indices are zero-based. Existing source/data/processes were not changed. All executable reproductions use CPU-only synthetic dependencies; no GPU training, actual benchmark execution, model inference or genuine sealed-result access was performed.
+
+The source snapshot and end-of-audit integrity comparison are in `source_identity.json` and `audit_scope.json`. The exact SFT local-copy designation comes from the user; `image_integrity.json` records each parquet SHA256 and verifies every embedded image against `img_sha`. The artifact has 92,229 train rows, 2,184 dev rows, 2,386 unique train QA endpoints and 5,448 weighted train QA final rows. The build removes the intended sets and preserves the expected final-goal construction. A separate pure-helper replay found one cached direct approval (`396#qa`, 3 hr 28 min versus answer2 3 hr 28) which the new comparator rejects; builder `DIRECT_OK` at `data/v4_build_parquet.py:70` trusts `ok` without recomputing this check. This is a verifier-consistency gap, not independent proof that its gold is wrong.
+
+`inspect_artifact.py` preserves the previous lexical answer classifier and population ordering. Seed 2026111802 draws four unique endpoints from each of ten strata, without rejecting previous samples. The original-kind strata contain 283/114/902/96/653 compound date-time/name/number/phrase/price endpoints and 36/13/163/9/117 question endpoints. Small name/phrase strata explain the ten repeated endpoints. `manual_judgments.json` was written after viewing all forty screenshots. `visual_review.json` carries the exact prompts, histories, locations, decisions, Wilson intervals and population-weighted estimates. Rates describe unique endpoints, not duplicated SFT rows. With only four observations per cell, corpus estimates are very uncertain; no statistically established improvement over the earlier audit is claimed.
+
+All 40 primary screenshots and eleven retained prior examples were viewed in full-resolution contact sheets. Five additional screenshots checked Gmail, Drive, a misleading Dropbox goal, Adidas inventory and the Xe control. These followups are outside primary rates. The Dropbox census candidate (`3439#qa`) actually uses TeraBox, which is installed: its defect is a wrong goal app, not proof that the used app is absent. The Adidas example (`15271#qa`, final train shard 12 row 5223) has an actual Adidas shoe screen and no Adidas entry. The original-kind question stratum still includes compound fallbacks; classification was not adjusted after viewing.
+
+The same app census is case-insensitive longest known app-pool name immediately followed by `app`, checked against the actual Installed apps line. It is a bounded lexical candidate census, not a package-identity audit. In contrast, builder `_POOL_RE` at `data/v4_build_parquet.py:138` is case-sensitive, excludes short names, and scans original goals before rewritten questions introduce additional names. All lists are stable within episodes; stability alone does not establish correctness.
+
+AW exposure scanning excludes Installed apps distractors and email-domain-only matches. The unchanged scanner yields train 70/dev 4; named Gmail/Drive/Maps/YouTube train 53/dev 2. The expanded scanner adds `Drive app` and similar display-name forms, yielding train 73/dev 4. Some broad calendar hits are widgets inside travel apps, not confirmed AW-app usage. Confirmed counterexamples include lowercase `gmail` in `12608#qa`, lowercase `google drive` in `2864#qa`, and the visually unmistakable Maps navigation screen in qa31, which has no named-app text hit. Builder `_CAP_APPS` at line 129 is case-sensitive; `aw_flag` at lines 167–174 checks original candidate goals, not eventual teacher questions. No copied benchmark task is established. Template scanning used only public local source, not outcome files: 57 class templates, 25 IR prompts and 18 dynamic-goal literal forms against 26,750 distinct built goals, with zero full-template or eight-word literal matches. Paraphrases/runtime composition remain untested.
+
+The published RL revision could not be retrieved: the new snapshot was not cached and the Hub API returned a DNS ConnectError. The web-tool fallback also could not access the endpoint. `census_and_pool.py` replays the unchanged `data/v4_rl_pool.py` selection, grouping and final NumPy permutation from real rebuilt rows: 700 QA final, 500 complete, 300 other and 500 click/long-press states. Calibration compares the older cached parquet's metadata/order and content SHA256 to the archived inventory, and all 2,000 replay positions match. This validates the replay algorithm; it does not establish that the publisher uploaded precisely these new bytes. Reconstructed pool order is explicit in every attack file. Published-pool checks remain incomplete.
+
+Reward fixtures pass, including previous magnitude/date/AM-PM/%/GB losses. The remaining `same_answer` weaknesses are executable: `CUR` at `data/v4_answer_check.py:32` requires word boundaries for ISO names, so `INR8,109.08` has no recognized INR currency; line 56 rejects currency differences only when both sides have recognized currencies. `essential()` omits `p` as a meridiem suffix. Line 65's shorter-word-subset rule permits arbitrary extra words, including `is incorrect`; `incorrect` is absent from `NEG`. All 639 numeric-bearing QA references accept the appended contradiction. Numeric stripping succeeds on 305/700; it is a probe-acceptance count, not a visual error count. Typing capitalization changes all reject (36 changed strings), but whitespace is still normalized by design. The coordinate function at `train/rl_reward.py:54–58` remains Gaussian distance to one annotated point and does not certify element membership or task success.
+
+`repro_wrappers.py` copies wrappers into new isolated fixtures, substitutes workspace roots and launcher placeholders, and stubs all network/GPU/emulator/process commands. `local_v4_to_aw.sh:34–38` still masks runner exit 42. `v4_gate.py:48–62` validates counts and equality between submitted task-name sets, not a frozen canonical identity set/seed/model; synthetic inputs with the current 136/80 counts still pass. RL evaluation/upload failures now accumulate and return exit 1; this fix is verified. The sealed-v2 fixture continues to fail closed and keeps its synthetic outcome inside its synthetic sealed log.
+
+`vm_rl_go.sh:17–35` still runs smoke before waiting unless SKIP_SMOKE=1 and an old RL DONE marker exists. No current VM environment or smoke timing was inspected. `vm_rl_go.sh:38` estimates step count from a four-step base-model smoke and forces a minimum of ten; probes show a 16,200-second allowance can yield 20,000 seconds of estimated optimization. There is no hard overall timeout for training/waits/evaluation/uploads. A historical smoke marker is not tied to data or code identity.
+
+`scripts/strict_dev_metrics.py:13` uses the lenient parser. A one-row prediction containing two concatenated objects yields answer_exact_strict=1, although the reward's strict parser rejects it. Line 19 counts any status, so status infeasible produces complete_status=1. Empty input files return exit 0. Neither this tool nor the RL launcher enforces expected canonical rows/manifests or the numeric promotion thresholds; `vm_rl_go.sh:58–66` only computes/uploads metrics, and does not invoke the seed-30 gate. `docs/PREREG_v4.md` now specifies +0.05 strict answer gain, <=0.03 false answers, >=-0.02 AC change, and the AW gate plus no loss of total successes. The rule is documented but is not an implemented promotion check. `vm_model_pipeline.sh:40–46` still accepts cached metrics by completeness/model without binding prompt/app-pool identity. Dev remains drawn from v3 train, held out only from v4; clean v3-versus-v4 held-out comparison is not established. The two old exchange-rate controls are absent; dev_complete 9070 still asks about the actual exchange rate, outside the new regex cue list.
+
+The unchanged `train/grpo_vlm.py:65–73` silently filters unknown config fields and does not enforce package versions. Lines 75–89 log rewards without rejecting zero-variance/truncated groups. Lines 111–122 load another CUDA model while the trainer/optimizer remain live, print generated text, and emit RL DONE without parsing the action. These are source risks, not observed GPU failures. The RL launcher still references unpinned `AndroidControl-screen-agent-sft@test`. `data/vm_v4_teacher.py:114` initializes fresh label dictionaries, and lines 176–192 process all ScreenQA batches before the next save; restart and incremental-checkpoint gaps therefore remain. Both teacher scripts, the GRPO runner, evaluation cache implementation and gate hashes are unchanged since the previous audit.
